# Bulk import rules

- Accept `.txt`, `.md`, `.rtf`, `.doc`, and `.docx` files.
- Extract every valid http/https URL with a robust regex (`findall`, not one-per-line `search`). Unescape Google Docs backslashes before scanning.
- Ignore empty lines. `#` comments without a URL are ignored; lines like `# https://…` still yield the URL. `#` headings, bold lines, and `Category:` / `Subject:` labels are categories.
- Heading lines without a URL set the project category for following links. The folder name is the first two words. The full heading is stored as `import_note`.
- The host picks the bucket: adult hosts under `downloads/porn/<category>/`; every other host under `downloads/<site>/<category>/` (`youtube`, `x.com`, `bbc.com`, …).
- A subject comes from non-URL link text, then a human slug in the path. A URL is never the job title. Skip listing and search URLs (`/search`, `/results`, `/tag/`, `/categories/`, `/feed`, `/explore`).
- Support: bare URLs (watch, /shorts/, youtu.be, query strings), markdown `[text](url)`, `Title | URL`, inline URLs, UTF-8 and UTF-16 files.
- Do not treat bare numbered markers (`1.`, `2)`) as titles.
- Dedupe against existing queue URLs and download archive.
- Always preview counts and require confirmation before enqueue. Never auto-start.
- Stamp `download_output_dir`, `download_category`, and `site_key` on enqueue.
